                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A brilliantly intense, raw, and delightfully chaotic retro VR shooter that throws you straight into the deep end! Standing your ground in a bleak sci-fi hangar while fending off endless hordes of grotesque alien monsters charging at you from every single angle is exactly as nerve-wracking as it sounds.The low-poly, unpolished visual style and the complete lack of a user interface capture that early-era virtual reality tech-demo aesthetic flawlessly. Swapping between high-powered lightning guns and devastating flamethrowers while managing your physical play space to dodge incoming projectiles creates a highly frantic, adrenaline-fueled, and unforgiving gameplay loop.It is the perfect, bite-sized arcade challenge for testing your sensory limits, burning off some energy in VR, and experiencing a piece of nostalgic, hard-as-nails indie action—all without spending a single penny. A rough, messy, but genuinely thrilling wave-defense game for anyone looking to push their reflexes to the absolute max. Definitely recommended!",
